0023 — a build's style table stays out of the framework directory.

Backport of upstream pocket-nexus/pocketjs#591 (586428b2, merged
2026-10-19), the style-table half only, with two departures. Pass 1 wrote
`framework/src/styles.generated.ts` — one gitignored file shared by every
build of the tree — and pass 2 resolved that path off disk. Now:

- `tools/build.ts` writes the style module to `<outdir>/<output>.styles.ts`
  and prints that path; nothing is written into the framework directory.
- `jsxPlugin`, given `generatedStyles`, resolves the framework's
  `styles.generated` import itself (upstream's `resolveImport` and filter),
  so pass 2 never asks the disk for it, and the `.tsx?` loader serves this
  build's table for that path from memory, as it already did at the pin.
- `framework/src/styles.generated.ts` is committed as the empty table that
  code importing framework sources without a build receives, and leaves
  `.gitignore`. Its `FONT_SLOTS` type carries `face?: string`, which is the
  shape `generateStylesModule` emits here after 0016.
- `tools/site-build.ts` drops the stub it seeded for the same reason, and
  `site/build.ts` bundles the playground runtimes with `dist/hero.styles.ts`
  rather than whichever table the last build left behind. Both as upstream.

Departure 1, the namespace. Upstream resolves the import into a
`pocketjs-generated-styles` namespace and loads it there. Bun names each
module in a bundle above its code — a file by its path relative to the
build's cwd, a namespaced module as `namespace:path` with the path as
given — so upstream's form prints `// pocketjs-generated-styles:/<the
checkout>/framework/src/styles.generated.ts` into every bundle, and the
bundle's bytes then depend on where the repository is checked out. No
bundle carried an absolute path before. Resolving to the same path in the
file namespace keeps the comment
`// vendor/pocketjs/framework/src/styles.generated.ts` and the module the
pin's loader produced: built from committed sources before and after this
patch, all 45 compositions in pocket-motion give byte-identical bundles and
paks.

Departure 2, a refusal. The interception compares the path an import names
with `GENERATED_STYLES_PATH` as strings, so a `styles.generated.ts` that
reaches the loader at any other path is an import that named another
file. Measured before adding it: Bun hands the plugin realpaths on both
sides, so a symlinked tree, a case-variant spelling on a case-insensitive
volume and `/tmp` against `/private/tmp` all intercept. A second FILE does
not — a copy of `framework/src` reached by a relative path, or any module
of that name — and was bundled from disk. With the committed empty table
`mount` then throws `unknown class ... (dynamic classes must be ternaries
of full literals)`, a diagnosis that points elsewhere; with a stale copy,
which is what the file held after any build before this patch, a red class
rendered blue and the build exited 0. The loader now throws naming both
paths.

Not ported: the transform cache's move to `~/.cache/pocket-nexus`
(`tools/targets/cache.ts`, `tools/psp-toolchain.ts`), a separate hunk of
`jsx-plugin.ts` that changes nothing about the style table; the
placeholder-renderer removal; `tests/build-writes.test.ts` and the e2e
install test, whose cache assertions need the cache move; and the
`site/content/docs` prose. The transform cache stays at
`.cache/transforms/`, content-addressed, and is the one thing a build still
writes inside the tree.

`GENERATED_STYLES_PATH` keeps the pin's `URL.pathname` rather than
upstream's later `fileURLToPath`. Every path in this file is spelled that
way at the pin, so a checkout under a path with a space already fails
before the style table matters (`ENOENT` on a percent-encoded
`framework/src/index.ts`); the refusal covers the comparison either way.

pocket-motion `tests/style-table.test.ts` holds each piece and goes red with
it removed: the build writing nothing in the tree but the transform cache,
the bundle naming no absolute path (red with upstream's namespace), a tree
with no style module on disk building (red without the `onResolve`:
`Could not resolve: "./styles.generated.ts"`), and the refusal.

When the pin moves past 586428b2 this patch is dropped, and both
departures have to be carried forward against upstream's form.

`git apply` skips everything above the first `diff --git`.
